I'm getting you to learn a very habitual process of templating.

414
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:11,240
如果长期坚持，你会养成很好的习惯，
If you do this over time, you're going to develop a very strong habit and, ultimately, some very good consistency.

417
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:16,780
现在，在进入下一部分前，
Now, before I move on, I mentioned something about a principle-based approach.

418
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:20,353
我想强调一个重要问题：很多课程都爱‘授人以鱼’。
What a lot of courses do, and this is important to highlight—

419
00:21:20,353 --> 00:21:24,496
what a lot of courses do is they want to give a man a fish.

421
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:25,400
我要原样写出来。
I'm going to write it like it.

422
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:32,680
他们就爱‘授人以鱼’。
They want to give a man a fish. Okay. Now, why I find this horribly wrong

423
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:35,725
问题是，‘授人以鱼’只能让他吃饱几小时或几天，但最终，他还是会面对同样的问题。
is that when we give a man a fish, ultimately,

424
00:21:35,725 --> 00:21:39,379
he'll be satisfied for a couple of hours, a couple of days,

425
00:21:39,379 --> 00:21:41,815
but eventually, he's stuck with the same problem.

427
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,560
交易也是一样。
And it's the same thing with regards to trading.

428
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:47,321
如果我把具体流程给你，‘好，把差值设为这个，
If I give you the exact process, and I tell you,

429
00:21:47,321 --> 00:21:50,333
'Okay, keep your difference to this, keep your minimum percentage to this.

430
00:21:50,333 --> 00:21:54,600
最低百分比设为这个，价格到这个位置就进场，止损放这里。’
When it gets to this exact price, you put it here, you put the exact stop there.'

432
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:57,077
如果我给你这个流程，猜猜看？
If I give you that process, well, guess what?

433
00:21:57,077 --> 00:21:59,607
市场肯定会变，100%，肯定会变
The markets are going to change. 100%, they're going to change.

434
00:21:59,607 --> 00:22:00,619
市场在不断变化。
They're constantly changing. Okay.

435
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:05,560
如果你没意识到市场在不断调整，
If you're not aware that markets constantly shift and adjust, then you're not observing them enough.

437
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:08,916
所以，重点是：我不想‘授人以鱼’。
So, the whole point is that I don't want to give you a fish.

438
00:22:08,916 --> 00:22:10,719
我想‘授人以渔’。
I want to give you a fishing rod.

439
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:14,845
最终，我想向你们展示每个策略背后的核心原则。
I want to show you, ultimately, what every strategy's underlying principles are.

440
00:22:14,845 --> 00:22:18,021
因为猜猜看？推动市场上涨或下跌的，
Because guess what? It's not the support or the resistance line

441
00:22:18,021 --> 00:22:20,619
并不是支撑位或阻力位本身。
that ultimately makes a market go up or down.

442
00:22:20,620 --> 00:22:26,340
而是围绕支撑位和阻力位的核心原则，才推动市场涨跌。
It's the underlying principles around that support and resistance that make the market go up and down.

445
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:37,140
比如，主动交易会推动市场激进上涨。被动交易则显示大量流动性被使用。
For example, initiative makes the market go up aggressively. Responsive shows us a high amount of liquidity being utilized.

447
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:43,480
平衡市场往往难以突破。失衡市场则展现良好的突破机会。
Balanced markets tend to struggle to break out. Imbalanced markets show us good breakout opportunities.

449
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:46,265
现在，掌握这些基本原则后，你不仅能采用我展示的策略，还能自己学会捕鱼。
Now, knowing these basic principles, ultimately,

450
00:22:46,265 --> 00:22:49,840
not only can you adopt the strategies I'm showing you,

451
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:53,773
But you can ultimately then learn to catch your own fish.

452
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:55,760
这正是本课程的目的。
And that's the purpose of this course.

453
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,300
目的就是教你这些原则。
The purpose is for me to teach you the principles.

454
00:22:58,300 --> 00:23:01,307
给你一个习惯化的流程，来学习和采纳这些原则，每一天，希望你不仅能采用我的策略，还能开发出自己的策略。
Give you a habitual process for learning and adopting

455
00:23:01,307 --> 00:23:03,980
those principles every single day, in hopes that

456
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:07,656
not only do you adopt my strategies, but learn your own.

458
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:10,460
现在开始讲解吧。
Let's get into that now.

459
00:23:10,540 --> 00:23:15,360
我们来聊聊拍卖失衡中的那些原则。
Let's talk about those principles that you're going to find within the auction imbalance.

461
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:19,440
强拍卖流程和弱拍卖流程。
So, strong and weak auction processes.

462
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:24,880
现在，我认为最好的开始方式，还是先画一个小失衡图。
Now, again, I think the best way to start is to just draw a little bit of an imbalance again.

464
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:28,660
我们来看10和100。
So, let's go 10 and 100.

465
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:35,700
我在这儿只画顶部，20。我要画得非常、非常——几乎有点夸张。
I'm just going to draw the top ones here, 20. I'm going to make it really, really—almost silly.

467
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:39,280
30和100，还有40。
30 and 100 and 40.

468
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:45,340
显然，我们能看到这些失衡。
So, we can see, obviously, the imbalances.

469
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:46,200
哦，回到之前。
Oh, let's go back.

470
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:48,260
所以，你们能看到那里的失衡。
So, you can see the imbalances there.

471
00:23:48,640 --> 00:23:51,260
我不想花太多时间画失衡图。
I don't want to spend too much time drawing out imbalances.

472
00:23:56,680 --> 00:23:57,980
好。所以，那里有失衡。
Alright. So, there are imbalances.

473
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:03,340
现在，首先要解读的是强拍卖流程和弱拍卖流程。
Now, ultimately, the first thing to interpret is a strong and weak auction process.

475
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:09,100
理论上，拍卖失衡就是强拍卖流程。
An auction imbalance is, in theory, a strong auction process.

476
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:14,969
然而，这是理解该策略最关键的一点，只有当失衡推动深色区域上涨时，它才是强拍卖流程。
However, and this is the most important thing

477
00:24:14,969 --> 00:24:16,993
to understanding this strategy,

478
00:24:16,993 --> 00:24:23,576
It's only a strong auction process if the imbalance is lifting dark colors.

479
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:27,440
这是真正的关键。
This is the real key.

480
00:24:27,620 --> 00:24:29,760
如果你发现一些深色块，
If you have some real dark colors

481
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:32,900
随着失衡形成，
as the imbalance is created, you’re getting some real dark shades

483
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:35,100
价格上涨时会出现深色阴影。
as we go up.

484
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:37,420
换句话说，真实的卖盘正被主动吃单。
In other words, real offers are being lifted.

485
00:24:37,780 --> 00:24:41,220
买方非常激进，正大量吞噬成交量。
The buyer is being that aggressive and is lifting very high amounts of volume.

487
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:44,920
这种失衡表明了强拍卖流程。
That sort of imbalance shows us a strong auction process.

488
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:48,560
而相反的情况，则是弱拍卖流程。
Now, the counter—or the flip of that—is a weak auction process.

490
00:24:48,700 --> 00:24:55,960
比如，失衡存在，但成交量可能只有20比70。
I.e., where we have an imbalance, but, for instance, maybe it’s only 20 by 70.

492
00:24:56,680 --> 00:25:04,140
换句话说，成交量很低。或1比6，或20比140。
In other words, it’s low amounts of volume. Or 1 by 6, or again, 20 by 140.

494
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:10,060
这比成交量很高的情况弱得多，
This is a far weaker auction process than, say, for example, we had much higher numbers.

496
00:25:10,060 --> 00:25:11,340
比如200、200、300手。
You have 200, 200, 300.

497
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,480
我等会儿会展示这两个例子。
I’ll show those two examples in a bit.

498
00:25:13,660 --> 00:25:16,000
但先理解基本前提：强拍卖流程。
But just understand that basic premise: a strong auction.

499
00:25:16,060 --> 00:25:20,740
我们在对角线方向上吞噬大量成交量。
We’re lifting high amounts of volume as we’re going in the diagonal way, of course.

501
00:25:21,420 --> 00:25:22,460
弱拍卖流程。
And a weak auction.

502
00:25:22,740 --> 00:25:25,700
同样是对角线，但我们只吞噬卖盘的少量成交量。
Again, diagonally, but we’re lifting very small amounts on the offer.

503
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:30,600
基本前提——经验法则：强拍卖不会立即反转。
Now, the basic premise—the rule of thumb: A strong auction won’t always reverse straight away.

505
00:25:30,700 --> 00:25:31,640
它可能会继续。
It’s likely to continue.

506
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:33,960
弱拍卖很可能会反转。
A weak auction will likely reverse.

507
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:36,536
我学到这个策略的地方——如果你长期交易德国国债，你会发现市场在中午左右会频繁出现翻转。
Now, where I learned this—actually, this strategy—was

508
00:25:36,536 --> 00:25:39,784
if you’ve been a German Bund trader for a long time,

509
00:25:39,784 --> 00:25:44,115
you’ll notice that a lot of flipping comes into the market around about lunchtime, midday.

510
00:25:44,360 --> 00:25:48,920
这种翻转通常看起来像弱拍卖失衡。
Now, this flipping very often will look like a weak auction imbalance.

512
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:51,053
所以，如果你想学会交易这个策略，最佳交易时机之一——比如在德国国债中——就是午餐时间。
So, if you want to learn to trade this,

513
00:25:51,053 --> 00:25:54,608
one of the best times to trade this—in, say, for instance, the German Bunds—

514
00:25:54,608 --> 00:25:55,319
is around lunchtime.

515
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:57,960
即欧洲时段的11点到1点。
So, 11 o’clock to 1 o’clock in the European session.

516
00:25:58,500 --> 00:26:03,360
我等会儿会讲解策略的变体。
Now, I’ll go through the variations of the strategy in a minute.

518
00:26:03,780 --> 00:26:06,220
但先聊聊其他原则。
But let’s just talk about some of the other principles.

519
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:09,080
现在，失衡市场与平衡市场。
Now, imbalanced versus balanced markets.

520
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:16,380
失衡市场——我总是说——是脱离平衡的市场。
So, an imbalanced market—again, as I always say—a market that’s out of balance.

522
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:20,551
比如，我们交易价格接近前一交易日的极值，甚至突破极值的任一侧。
So, i.e., we’re trading relatively close to the previous day’s extreme,

523
00:26:20,551 --> 00:26:23,156
or even outside of the extreme on either side.

525
00:26:23,180 --> 00:26:28,400
对我来说，在这些极值点更易看到强拍卖失衡。
For me, you tend to see much stronger auction imbalances at those extreme points.

526
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:30,960
我会更谨慎地反向操作这些失衡。
I’d be far more cautious to fade those.

527
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:34,240
不过别担心。我会给你一个精确策略，
But again, don’t worry. I’m going to show you an exact strategy

528
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:36,160
告诉你何时反向、如何反向、为何反向。
of how to fade, when to fade, and why to fade.

529
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:40,720
在失衡市场中，我们更可能看到更多失衡。
So, in an imbalanced market, we are likely to see more of these imbalances.

531
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:47,175
而在平衡市场中，当我们交易在前一交易日区间中点时，我们更可能看到弱拍卖失衡，而这类失衡往往会自行反转。
Whereas, in a balanced market, where we’re trading smack in the middle of the previous day’s range,

532
00:26:47,175 --> 00:26:49,775
we are likely to see more weaker-type imbalances,

533
00:26:49,775 --> 00:26:52,700
which, as I said, tend to reverse upon themselves.

536
00:26:53,260 --> 00:26:56,720
现在，注意：我提到了高成交量和低成交量。
Now, note: I’ve mentioned the high and low volume.

537
00:26:56,800 --> 00:26:58,980
这是一个关键支点，你等一下就能看到。
That is a key pivot, as you will see.

538
00:26:59,280 --> 00:27:02,900
还有Delta。所以，我们要关注的两个关键指标是
Also, the delta. So, the two key metrics we’re going to pay attention to

539
00:27:02,900 --> 00:27:05,920
成交量、Delta，当然还有阴影。
are the volume, the delta, and, obviously, the shading.

540
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:10,160
我认为阴影非常重要，因为它能展示相对位移。
I think the shading is really, really important, because that’s going to show us the relative shift.

542
00:27:10,560 --> 00:27:16,120
这三个是我们在示例中要关注的关键指标。
And those are the three key metrics we’re going to pay attention to when we get to the examples.

544
00:27:16,240 --> 00:27:23,534
强拍卖失衡时，我们期望看到深色阴影、高成交量和高相对Delta。
We expect to see dark shading for strong auction imbalances, high volume for strong auction imbalances, and high relative delta.

546
00:27:23,534 --> 00:27:23,898
为什么？
Why?

547
00:27:23,980 --> 00:27:25,940
因为我们在大量吃卖单。
Because we’re lifting very big offers.

548
00:27:26,620 --> 00:27:30,620
而弱拍卖的情况相反，我们通常看不到太多深色阴影。
And, obviously, the flip for weak auctions, we won’t tend to see much dark shading.

550
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:35,200
成交量会相对正常且低迷，Delta也几乎不会变化。
Volume will be relatively normal and muted, and the delta will hardly shift.

552
00:27:36,080 --> 00:27:40,480
现在，关于失衡为何发生，这一点很重要。
Now, in terms of why this imbalance occurs, this is quite important.

553
00:27:40,600 --> 00:27:43,731
有时失衡是因为止损触发。
Sometimes an imbalance can occur because of stops.

554
00:27:43,731 --> 00:27:48,819
可能市场到达某个点位，突然出现止损单被触发。
Maybe the market reaches a certain point, and suddenly we get a stop-out.

556
00:27:48,820 --> 00:27:51,420
止损触发的失衡确实倾向于回补。为什么？
Stop-out imbalances do tend to fill out. Why?

557
00:27:51,900 --> 00:27:53,934
因为，自然地，当市场触发止损时，显然只是因为一个订单试图退出市场。
Because, naturally, when a market stops out,

558
00:27:53,934 --> 00:27:58,876
obviously it’s stopping out simply because one order is trying to get out of the market.

560
00:27:58,900 --> 00:28:01,300
所以，这些失衡确实倾向于回补。
So, those imbalances do tend to fill out.

561
00:28:02,580 --> 00:28:07,831
失衡的另一个原因是市场出现某些关键基本面。
Another reason for imbalances is when we get some key fundamentals in the market.

562
00:28:07,831 --> 00:28:13,833
同样，这些失衡不一定会被填平。为什么？因为这些基本面可能特别重要。
Again, these don’t have to fill out. Why? Because those fundamentals can be particularly important.

563
00:28:13,833 --> 00:28:16,458
因为市场中出现了主动性交易。
is because of initiative in the market.

565
00:28:16,520 --> 00:28:19,113
稍后我们会深入讲解这个策略。
We will talk quite extensively about this strategy a little later on.

566
00:28:19,113 --> 00:28:22,139
这是导致拍卖失衡的第三个原因。
That’s one of the third reasons why we tend to get this imbalance.

568
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:31,645
有时我们会认为止损只出现在极端位置。
Sometimes we assume stops only occur at an extreme.

569
00:28:31,645 --> 00:28:35,599
其实不是。止损可能出现在区间中间。
They don’t. Stops can occur in the middle of a range.

570
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:39,843
如果存在某些仓位分布，比如我之前在某个策略中展示的，有支撑、支撑失效和阻力位的情况，
If there's some positioning, like I showed you in one of the strategies earlier,

571
00:28:39,843 --> 00:28:41,924
with the support, failed support, and resistance,

572
00:28:41,924 --> 00:28:45,493
you can have an auction imbalance in the middle of the range.

574
00:28:45,500 --> 00:28:50,494
同样，当Delta解绑时，你会再次看到止损在区间中间被触发。
Equally, when we get to the point of a delta unwind,

575
00:28:50,494 --> 00:28:56,396
you’ll see again some stop-outs in the middle of the range occurring.

577
00:28:56,400 --> 00:29:03,060
这是拍卖失衡流程中最重要的原则。
the most important principles of the imbalance process.

579
00:29:03,060 --> 00:29:09,940
了解失衡的变体形式，然后才能开始制定策略。
what the variations are going to look like, and then we can start to develop a strategy approach.

582
00:29:10,380 --> 00:29:17,180
交易策略中，背景非常重要。
Context matters a lot in terms of the trade strategy.

583
00:29:17,180 --> 00:29:23,380
你识别出一个失衡后，要放到背景中：
you look at an imbalance and identify it, you put it into the context: Where is it trading right now?

585
00:29:23,380 --> 00:29:24,620
它为什么会出现？
Why has it occurred?

586
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:30,540
是止损吗？是基本面消息吗？还是仅仅成交量低？
Is it stops? Is it just a fundamental piece of news? Or is it just low volume?

588
00:29:30,540 --> 00:29:36,940
一定要解读失衡出现的背后原因。
Always interpret the context behind why that imbalance is occurring in the first place.

590
00:29:37,040 --> 00:29:40,754
首先，如我所述，你可以设置最小差值。
The first thing to observe, as I said, is you can have a minimum difference.

591
00:29:40,754 --> 00:29:42,239
其次是百分比。
The second thing is the percentage.

593
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:51,720
也就是说，100手到400手之间，如果我设置400%或更高，就会形成失衡。
In other words, between 100 contracts and 400 contracts, that will create an imbalance if I set it to 400% or bigger.

595
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:55,368
这里没有对错之分，但我想说的是，失衡阈值别低于200%，也别高于400%。
There is no right or wrong in this,

596
00:29:55,368 --> 00:30:01,296
but what I would say is, don’t go less than 200% for imbalances,

597
00:30:01,296 --> 00:30:04,034
and don’t go more than 400%.

598
00:30:04,540 --> 00:30:13,220
否则，你可能会错过很多信息。
Otherwise, you could be missing out on a lot of information.

600
00:30:13,560 --> 00:30:20,076
如果低于200%，你可能包含了太多信息。
If you go less than 200%, you could be including too much information.

601
00:30:20,076 --> 00:30:26,049
这个参数的目的就是提取有意义的信息—只提取你最终想知道的信息。
The whole point of that setting is to extract meaningful information—

602
00:30:26,049 --> 00:30:31,479
only take out the information you ultimately want to know.

604
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:35,160
是否需要单独的图表？这取决于情况。
Should you have a separate chart? This depends.

605
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:43,860
当然，在单独图表上更容易观察，因为它只在失衡出现时显示颜色。
It is easier to see on a separate chart, of course, because it only shows color where an imbalance occurs.

